2026-09-27T12:05:54.9472882Z Description:
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9473379Z This PPA contains more recent Python versions packaged for Ubuntu.
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9473791Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9474768Z Disclaimer: there's no guarantee of timely updates in case of security problems or other issues. If you want to use them in a security-or-otherwise-critical environment (say, on a production server), you do so at your own risk.
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9475825Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9475949Z Update Note
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9476266Z ===========
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9476673Z Please use this repository instead of ppa:fkrull/deadsnakes.
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9477053Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9477234Z Reporting Issues
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9477644Z ================
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9477823Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9478263Z Issues can be reported in the master issue tracker at:
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9478811Z https://github.com/deadsnakes/issues/issues
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9479108Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9479314Z Supported Ubuntu and Python Versions
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9479736Z ====================================
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9480043Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9480231Z - Ubuntu 22.04 (jammy) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.10)
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9480778Z - Ubuntu 24.04 (noble) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.12)
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9481345Z - Ubuntu 26.04 (resolute) Python3.7+ (NOT Python3.14)
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9482202Z - Note: Python 3.10 (jammy), Python3.12 (noble), Python3.14 (resolute) are not provided by deadsnakes as upstream ubuntu provides those packages.
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9482856Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9483088Z Why some packages aren't built:
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9483791Z - Note: for 22.04+, older python versions requre libssl<3 so they are not currently built
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9484512Z - If you need these, reach out to asottile to set up a private ppa
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9484934Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9485319Z The packages may also work on other versions of Ubuntu or Debian, but that is not tested or supported.
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9485850Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9486009Z Packages
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9486364Z ========
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9486552Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9488631Z The packages provided here are loosely based on the debian upstream packages with some modifications to make them more usable as non-default pythons and on ubuntu.  As such, the packages follow debian's patterns and often do not include a full python distribution with just `apt install python#.#`.  Here is a list of packages that may be useful along with the default install:
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9490234Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9490526Z - `python#.#-dev`: includes development headers for building C extensions
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9491199Z - `python#.#-venv`: provides the standard library `venv` module
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9492180Z - `python#.#-distutils`: provides the standard library `distutils` module
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9493027Z - `python#.#-lib2to3`: provides the `2to3-#.#` utility as well as the standard library `lib2to3` module
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9493785Z - `python#.#-gdbm`: provides the standard library `dbm.gnu` module
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9494408Z - `python#.#-tk`: provides the standard library `tkinter` module
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9494945Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9495115Z Third-Party Python Modules
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9495514Z ==========================
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9495755Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9497517Z Python modules in the official Ubuntu repositories are packaged to work with the Python interpreters from the official repositories. Accordingly, they generally won't work with the Python interpreters from this PPA. As an exception, pure-Python modules for Python 3 will work, but any compiled extension modules won't.
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9499423Z 
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9500257Z To install 3rd-party Python modules, you should use the common Python packaging tools.  For an introduction into the Python packaging ecosystem and its tools, refer to the Python Packaging User Guide:
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9501317Z https://packaging.python.org/installing/
2026-09-27T12:05:54.9501669Z 
